    shimmy the target

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## THE ROOFTOPS (`story.ni:8832-8961`) — forward-only, east to the estate.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## A room's `first time` block is its whole first-visit description, so the
## climb text, the description and the source's `[first time]` tail (Bobby's
## virtues) sit in it together; later looks get the description alone.

create the Rooftop
  a room
  aka rooftops, main rooftop, roof, roofs, peaks, peak, valleys, valley, mountain range, landscape
  east to the Rooftop Edge
  down is blocked: rooftop-no-climbing-down
  up is blocked: rooftop-as-high-as-it-goes
  north is blocked: rooftop-focus-east
  south is blocked: rooftop-focus-east
  west is blocked: rooftop-focus-east
  northeast is blocked: rooftop-focus-east
  northwest is blocked: rooftop-focus-east
  southeast is blocked: rooftop-focus-east
  southwest is blocked: rooftop-focus-east
  first time
    You give the pipe a few experimental tugs, then take a deep breath and
    start shimmying up. The rain gutter squeaks and groans in protest. Your
    fingers cramp and your toes scrabble to find purchase on the rough
    bricks. Finally, three stories up, you grab the edge of the rooftop and
    haul yourself over.

    The rooftops are like a miniature mountain range up here, with peaks and
    valleys sloping away into the distance. Chimneys and stovepipes stand
    sentry like the keeps and towers of castles. Bobby has exclaimed the
    virtues of rooftop travel before, and finally you see what he was going
    on about. It feels like you could explore forever up here.

  The rooftops are like a miniature mountain range up here, with peaks and
  valleys sloping away into the distance. Chimneys and stovepipes stand
  sentry like the keeps and towers of castles.

define phrase rooftop-no-climbing-down
  It took quite an effort to get up here. You're not climbing back down until
  you find what Bobby told you to find... the letter in Fossville's mansion.
end phrase

define phrase rooftop-as-high-as-it-goes
  You're on the rooftops already; this is as high as you can go.
end phrase

define phrase rooftop-focus-east
  You need to focus on getting to Fossville's mansion, and if memory serves,
  that's east of here.
end phrase

## `story.ni:8871-8959`. Every planar direction but east refuses; the
## northeast and southeast are the drop (the source's facing lines).

create the Rooftop Edge
  a room
  aka edge, rooftops, roof, roofs, landscape, end, peaks, valleys, mountain range
  east to the Balcony
  up is blocked: rooftop-as-high-as-it-goes
  down is blocked: edge-deadly-fall
  northeast is blocked: edge-three-story-drop
  southeast is blocked: edge-three-story-drop
  north is blocked: edge-tantalizing
  south is blocked: edge-tantalizing
  west is blocked: edge-tantalizing
  northwest is blocked: edge-tantalizing
  southwest is blocked: edge-tantalizing

  The rooftop landscape ends here at a wide street dividing Commerce Street
  from the more affluent residential district that borders it. Far, far
  below, you can see all the little people going about their business.

define phrase edge-deadly-fall
  The only way down from here is a long, deadly fall.
end phrase

define phrase edge-three-story-drop
  The rooftops end that way in a three-story drop.
end phrase

define phrase edge-tantalizing
  The thought of exploring the roofs is tantalizing, but you need to focus on
  Bobby's mission first.
end phrase

