## `jump [direction]` / `jump to the balcony` (`story.ni:8919-8925`): the bare
## forms are a story action, the targeted forms ride the entering action so
## the balcony's own clause answers them.

define action jumping
  grammar
    jump
    jump over
    jump across
    jump east
    jump the gap
    leap
    leap over
    leap across
  refuse when the player is in the Balcony: balcony-no-jumping-back
  the player must be in the Rooftop Edge: jump-nowhere
  move the player to the Balcony

extend action entering
  grammar
    jump to the target
    jump over to the target
    jump across to the target
    jump on the target
    jump onto the target
    sit on the target
    sit down on the target
    sit the target

## DAVID: the source has no jump refusal away from the gap (there is no
## jumping action outside it); this is the one line the port needs.

define phrase jump-nowhere
  (TODO during play-testing — a jump anywhere but the rooftop's edge: no
  source line exists; David's.)
