## The jump (`story.ni:8905-8909`) is the Balcony's first-time prose: going
## east from the Rooftop Edge, `jump`, `enter balcony` all land here, once.

create the Balcony
  a room
  aka roof of black gate estate, roof, ornate balcony, western edge
  northeast to the Rooftop Garden
  southeast to the Patio
  west is blocked: balcony-no-jumping-back
  northwest is blocked: balcony-no-jumping-back
  southwest is blocked: balcony-no-jumping-back
  first time
    You peer across the gap at the balcony, judging the distance. About ten
    feet. Maybe a little bit more than ten feet. And it's slightly below you,
    which is a plus.

    Still, it's a really far jump.

    This is where Bobby told you to go. A letter... secrets about your
    father, he said. The thought of facing Bobby when he gets out, after they
    beat him up so bad, and telling him you were too scared to do what he
    asked you to do...

    You take a few steps back, run... and jump.

    The railing slams into your chest, knocking the breath out of you. Your
    feet pedal madly in empty air. You wrap your arms around the railing,
    trying to grab on, but you're slipping...

    Then your foot finds the edge of the balcony, and you push yourself up
    and over.

    You're standing on a balcony, complete with ornate railing, that runs
    along the roof's western edge. To the northeast is a garden; to the
    southeast, a patio.

  You're standing on a balcony, complete with ornate railing, that runs along
  the roof's western edge. To the northeast is a garden; to the southeast, a
  patio.

define phrase balcony-no-jumping-back
  If at all possible, you'd much rather find an escape route that doesn't
  involve death-defying leaps over fifty-foot drops. Besides, you can't leave
  until you find the letter Bobby was talking about.
end phrase

create the railing
  aka rail, railings, curved railing, elegant railing, ornate railing, marble, gilt iron, gilt, iron, white marble
  scenery
  in the Balcony

  The curved, elegant railing is made of white marble and gilt iron.

