## `turn winch`/`turn crank` (`story.ni:9220-9236`): the platform's turning
## consults the entity's own clause, so the turn rides one trait on both
## the winch and its crank. The source's push/pull on the crank is not
## carried: the platform refuses pushing scenery before any clause runs.

## The flip reads the state it just changed (statements run in sequence),
## so it pivots through `turning`: raised → turning → lowered, lowered →
## raised, each arm's line spoken on the state it lands in. (`select on the
## gaudy chandelier` / `when raised` ran no arm at all — GH #370.)

define trait winch-crank
  on the player turning
    change the gaudy chandelier to turning when the gaudy chandelier is raised
    change the gaudy chandelier to raised when the gaudy chandelier is lowered
    phrase winch-winds-the-rope when the gaudy chandelier is raised
    change the gaudy chandelier to lowered when the gaudy chandelier is turning
    phrase winch-lowers-the-rope when the gaudy chandelier is lowered
  end on

end trait

